CODEX-AUDIT/

# Local audit run output. Generated, never source: the 23 .py files it drops carry their own
# lint debt (66 ruff errors) and were being counted against the repo, so `ruff check .` locally
# reported 151 errors where CI's tracked-tree view saw 85. Ruff honours .gitignore, so ignoring
# it here is what makes a local lint run agree with CI. A project must not be graded on its own
# generated artifacts, and it must not be linted on them either.
.vool-audit/

# VOOL-DELIVERY bookkeeping: track the state files, but never the local approval artifact,
# transient evidence, or local-only scratch. The state files themselves are the source of truth.
VOOL-DELIVERY/GO_APPROVAL.json
VOOL-DELIVERY/evidence/*
!VOOL-DELIVERY/evidence/.gitkeep
VOOL-DELIVERY/*.local
VOOL-DELIVERY/PUBLIC_RELEASE_MANIFEST.json

# Accidental databases named from a Python object repr (illegal on NTFS, breaks Windows checkout)
*_PooledConnection*
<*>

